  "content": {
    "id": "p18-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "Factorise each of the following expressions:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p18-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$2x^4-x^2-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x-1)(x+1)(2x^2+1)$\n\nUse $y=x^2$, then factorise the difference of squares.",
          "worked": "Let $y=x^2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2y^2-y-1&=(2y+1)(y-1)\\\\2x^4-x^2-1&=(2x^2+1)(x^2-1)\\\\2x^4-x^2-1&=(2x^2+1)(x-1)(x+1)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$4x^4-5x^2+1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x-1)(x+1)(2x-1)(2x+1)$\n\nUse $y=x^2$, then factorise both differences of squares.",
          "worked": "Let $y=x^2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}4y^2-5y+1&=(4y-1)(y-1)\\\\4x^4-5x^2+1&=(4x^2-1)(x^2-1)\\\\4x^4-5x^2+1&=(2x-1)(2x+1)(x-1)(x+1)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$9x^4-10x^2+1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x-1)(x+1)(3x-1)(3x+1)$\n\nUse $y=x^2$, then factorise both differences of squares.",
          "worked": "Let $y=x^2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}9y^2-10y+1&=(9y-1)(y-1)\\\\9x^4-10x^2+1&=(9x^2-1)(x^2-1)\\\\9x^4-10x^2+1&=(3x-1)(3x+1)(x-1)(x+1)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q3-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$4x^4+3x^2-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(2x-1)(2x+1)(x^2+1)$\n\nUse $y=x^2$, then factorise the difference of squares.",
          "worked": "Let $y=x^2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}4y^2+3y-1&=(4y-1)(y+1)\\\\4x^4+3x^2-1&=(4x^2-1)(x^2+1)\\\\4x^4+3x^2-1&=(2x-1)(2x+1)(x^2+1)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q3-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$4x^4+3x^2-27$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(4x^2-9)(x^2+3)=(2x-3)(2x+3)(x^2+3)$\n\nUse $y=x^2$, then factorise the difference of squares.",
          "worked": "Let $y=x^2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}4y^2+3y-27&=(4y-9)(y+3)\\\\4x^4+3x^2-27&=(4x^2-9)(x^2+3)\\\\4x^4+3x^2-27&=(2x-3)(2x+3)(x^2+3)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q3-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$4x^4-13x^2+3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(2x-1)(2x+1)(x-\\sqrt{3})(x+\\sqrt{3})$\n\nUse $y=x^2$, then factorise both differences of squares.",
          "worked": "Let $y=x^2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}4y^2-13y+3&=(4y-1)(y-3)\\\\4x^4-13x^2+3&=(4x^2-1)(x^2-3)\\\\4x^4-13x^2+3&=(2x-1)(2x+1)(x^2-3)\\\\4x^4-13x^2+3&=(2x-1)(2x+1)(x-\\sqrt{3})(x+\\sqrt{3})\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      }
    ]
  },
